message:
Suggested fixes from PR discussion

@istfer Warning if ask for more cores than available and drop to max
number of cores.

@bpbond @dlebauer Throw a warning and proceed without parallelization if
`parallel=TRUE` but `parallel` package is not installed.

1) using Bety info from settings object;
2) grab paths of those .clim files that are already extracted during the previous runs;
3) splitting the processes of writing into Bety, right now it only contains two parts: initializing DB query elements and iteratively writing them into Bety;
4) adding new features to use more model-specific functions than met2model.SIPNET

update zenodo.json

tried to fix broken builds https://zenodo.org/account/settings/github/repository/PecanProject/pecan# causing this error:

```
{
    "status": 400, 
    "message": "Validation error.", 
    "errors": [
        {
            "field": "metadata.metadata", 
            "message": "Unknown field name."
        }
    ]
}
```

Probably also a good time to add any new contributors and update affiliations

